1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,760
past 2 a.m. in my apartment where i live alone

2
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:20,520
a high school boy who's my gaming friend

3
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:28,480
and me with my 100 degree fever

4
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:58,460
and me with my 100 degree fever

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:30,980
To be continued...

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:37,840
Hospital? Oh, mm-hmm. Yamada took me to a hospital that's open even at night. I'll be going back there tomorrow.

7
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:45,680
Huh? Oh, yeah. Well, you see, Yamada came to make sure I was okay last night and...

8
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:49,540
Huh? You haven't been dating this boy behind my back, have you?

9
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:53,540
No, of course not. We're just friends. He's really such a good person.

10
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:57,780
Uh, what? Wait, doesn't that mean...

11
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:01,840
I'll drop it until she's healthy again.

12
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:07,420
Well, that's about it for today. So I'm out of here, okay?

13
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:10,540
Thanks a bunch. Wait here while I get my wallet.

14
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:17,400
A man wouldn't really do that much for a woman he's not in love with, would he?

15
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:21,680
I don't think they would, but I don't know anything about Yamada's personality.

16
00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:27,660
As for Akane, after that heartbreak, it doesn't seem like she'll be falling in love again anytime soon.

17
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:37,100
All right, Akane, I'm heading out, but let me know right away if anything happens, okay?

18
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:37,960
Sure.

19
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:41,620
Hmm?

20
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,600
Remember, timing's everything when it comes to love.

21
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:49,620
Uh, right. That's true.

22
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:53,020
As long as you get that, fine. See you!

23
00:03:53,020 --> 00:04:21,020
I'll thank him properly when I'm better.

24
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:23,380
What should I do?

25
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:36,260
Hey, are you doing all right?

26
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,900
Runa can log in this weekend if you want to hang.

27
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,280
When you're well again, let's play together, okay?

28
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,280
Oh, Runa.

29
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:47,760
Come to think of it, did Runa end up logging in yesterday?

30
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:54,320
We were going to introduce ourselves to our new guild mate, but I haven't gotten a chance to meet her yet.

31
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:59,180
I'm worn out from studying, so maybe I'll play Phos for a bit.

32
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:07,620
I know Runa and Yamada won't be online, but maybe Ruhime and Mr. Kamoto will be free. I'd love to go hunting with them.

33
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:14,860
I haven't been leveling up much lately, so I want to get a lot done today.

34
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,960
Hey, it's Akanechi!

35
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:18,980
Hmm?

36
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:23,900
Oh, hey! The new player is here!

37
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:26,960
Come and meet our new guild member, Tsubaki!

38
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,600
It's so nice to meet you!

39
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:30,220
I'm Akane!

40
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:31,920
I'm a level 55 paladin!

41
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:32,980
I'm Tsubaki.

42
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:34,820
It's nice to meet you, too.

43
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:37,480
I just started playing, so I'm still new.

44
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:41,740
Before you arrived, I was asking Tsubaki to join me for some map reconnaissance.

45
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:44,760
But since you're here, Akanechi, maybe we should all go hunting?

46
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:45,880
I'd love to!

47
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:47,720
Huh? Hey, um...

48
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:52,060
I still have no idea how any of my abilities work yet, so I'd only get in your way right now.

49
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:55,900
If you're looking to learn your moves, our paladin, Akanechi, can show you!

50
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,840
So you're a paladin, too, Tsubaki?

51
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:00,460
I guess most players go for the mage class.

52
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:05,660
This place is full of wizards that can inflict ungodly amounts of damage.

53
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:08,840
Not only that, but everyone has higher defense than me.

54
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:13,460
To be honest, there are times when I wonder why I chose this job class in the first place.

55
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:16,920
I mean, they said they recommend this class for newbies.

56
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,720
But, you know, I think paladins unlock their true potential at the higher levels.

57
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:25,400
After all, they're the only job that can solo run bosses from endgame content.

58
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:28,900
It seems it'll be rewarding, so I really like it.

59
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:29,760
Ooh!

60
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:32,360
What a nice girl!

61
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:35,220
But I did hear that the role is hard to master.

62
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:36,240
Not to worry!

63
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:37,600
Just leave it to me!

64
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,600
I have to show her what I'm made of.

65
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:43,020
I have to make sure that I don't drag her down.

66
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:45,020
Hey, Mama!

67
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,280
Runa can't find her donuts anywhere!

68
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,980
Okay, shall we head out?

69
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:52,280
Is everyone's equipment ready for battle?

70
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:52,820
Yes.

71
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:54,300
And yes!

72
00:06:54,300 --> 00:07:03,600
The sky's so beautiful!

73
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:09,380
Like, the graphics for the sky in this game are so amazing, aren't they?

74
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,680
Personally, I think it might be my favorite part about Foss.

75
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,300
How do you feel about it, you two?

76
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:18,820
Sorry, Master!

77
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:20,400
We're a little busy right now!

78
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:20,600
Oh!

79
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:21,340
Strike!

80
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:21,980
Strike!

81
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:22,360
Strike!

82
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:22,700
Strike!

83
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:23,360
Strike!

84
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:23,440
Strike!

85
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:31,280
Anyway, can you help us out with this monster instead of taking in the scenery?

86
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,280
No matter what we do, it just won't die!

87
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:36,060
If Booty were to step in, my attack would kill it instantly!

88
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:39,200
It's not that strong of a boss, so give it all you've got!

89
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:40,640
You've got to be kidding me!

90
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:44,060
This giant blob of HP is so beefy, it's got four whole bars of health!

91
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:54,780
It's so amusing that the damage you're both dealing is less than the enemy's healing ability!

92
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,720
Hey, here it comes!

93
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,100
But...

94
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:08,100
It's true that...

95
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,740
This is getting us nowhere!

96
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,780
Thanks to the Master's recovery magic, we're not going to die, but...

97
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:14,820
It's...

98
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:15,380
It's...

99
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:16,120
It's...

100
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,120
It's...

101
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,340
It's...

102
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:18,920
It's...

103
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,800
It's...

104
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:22,400
Our morale is getting utterly destroyed like this!

105
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:25,440
You guys got this, you just gotta figure it out!

106
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:28,460
With some adjustments, you can totally subdue this boss at your level!

107
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:28,920
Huh?

108
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,080
Oh, I think I get it now!

109
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:33,860
Maybe we should just start mashing our skill buttons like crazy!

110
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:37,380
But that's what I've been doing since we started this fight!

111
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:40,500
How about we give the mash it to death strategy a shot?

112
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,780
Three, two...

113
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:42,040
...

114
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:59,760
They must be pounding like there's no tomorrow.

115
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,660
Would you guys like me to give you a clue?

116
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,060
Hold on. I understand now. I think.

117
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:06,680
Really?

118
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:09,180
Maybe. Please don't give us the answer yet.

119
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:09,920
Okay.

120
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:38,140
My fingers are dead.

121
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,000
So are mine.

122
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:43,260
But you know, we managed to chip away a lot in the second half.

123
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:47,480
It's almost like we had a certain amount of time to land our attacks at points.

124
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:50,060
Yeah, you're right. Like when he flapped his wings.

125
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:54,440
So maybe to make our attacks more efficient, we should try inflicting damage during that window.

126
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:56,320
Then we can unload on him with our skills.

127
00:09:56,860 --> 00:10:00,000
Before we go again, how about we both read what our skills can do?

128
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:02,080
Good idea. And let's check our gear too.

129
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:05,040
Best of friends are ready.

130
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:24,900
My new guildmate Akane.

131
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:28,180
Akane. I assume she's most likely that Akane.

132
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:30,420
Huh?

133
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:36,600
She was pretty easy to talk to.

134
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:47,800
Yes?

135
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,060
Yes.

136
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:53,020
Huh?

137
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:55,380
What's a brutal D-metal?

138
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,460
I've never heard of it.

139
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:01,480
You know, the boss in the first meadow outside Phos' town of beginnings?

140
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:03,840
The big enemy that has four bars of HP?

141
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,840
Are you referring to the random spawning boss?

142
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:07,840
Yeah, that's it.

143
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,480
Rurihime said the same thing.

144
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:11,660
Have you ever defeated that one, Yamada?

145
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,980
I haven't battled that many bosses in that tier.

146
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:18,460
Oh, I see.

147
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:21,220
I was hoping you'd have some strategies or something.

148
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:26,660
Uh, well if it has some kind of gimmick, maybe you should try timing your moves to it?

149
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:29,320
A gimmick? Huh.

150
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:33,720
Like if there's a period when attacks are invalid, there are all kinds of patterns.

151
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,200
Oh yeah, he had one of those.

152
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,820
So when that happens, what should I do?

153
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,160
Oh, a buff!

154
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,440
That makes sense!

155
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:47,140
So, do you think you're gonna like our guild?

156
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:48,100
Huh?

157
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,360
And Akanechi!

158
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,700
She's pretty easy to talk to, right?

159
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:53,520
Uh, she is.

160
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:57,060
The fact that everyone is so nice has really put me at ease.

161
00:11:57,680 --> 00:12:00,140
Actually, I kind of started feeling bad about it.

162
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:00,960
Hmm?

163
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:02,440
But why is that?

164
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:04,720
Originally,

165
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,920
I wasn't all that interested in playing this game.

166
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:09,580
And to be frank,

167
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:13,440
I only asked to join the guild for reasons that were purely selfish.

168
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:16,460
But now that I'm getting into it,

169
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:20,560
I'm wondering what it was that I was trying to accomplish in the first place.

170
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:22,080
Are you okay?

171
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,540
Rudy would be happy to listen if you want to share.

172
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:37,800
All I ever did was look at him.

173
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:43,960
Just keeping to myself from afar like a coward.

174
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,140
It's nothing, really.

175
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:51,700
It's just that I lack courage and can't make a move.

176
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:58,800
Um, I'm not sure what it's all about.

177
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:01,360
But maybe start by taking some kind of action.

178
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:02,740
Even if it's small.

179
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:05,400
If there's something you really want to do,

180
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:07,240
then I said you should just do it anyway.

181
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:11,220
Waiting for the courage and motivation to well up will get you nowhere.

182
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,240
You have to take that first step.

183
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:16,000
If there's something you want to change.

184
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:22,400
So, yeah.

185
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:23,620
Oh, wow.

186
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:24,480
Look at the time.

187
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:27,080
Sorry for going on and on like that.

188
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,200
You must be wiped.

189
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:29,060
Yes.

190
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:30,360
My hand got numb,

191
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:31,540
so I switched to Bluetooth.

192
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,100
Honest as ever.

193
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:34,540
So in the end,

194
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,560
what were you asking me again?

195
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:37,180
Oh.

196
00:13:37,180 --> 00:13:38,860
Right.

197
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,860
It wasn't so much a question.

198
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:44,500
I just wanted to hear your voice.

199
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,440
I guess that's all.

200
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:47,260
Bye.

201
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:59,180
My hands are...

202
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:00,820
trembling.

203
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,920
Hey, Momo.

204
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:11,360
Thanks for today.

205
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:13,400
Can you talk now?

206
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:15,060
Yeah.

207
00:14:15,380 --> 00:14:16,860
Well, uh...

208
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,180
You see,

209
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:21,500
there's something I really want to talk to you about.

210
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:38,180
So, this is it.

211
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,460
I didn't know this place existed.

212
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:51,360
Anyway,

213
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:54,820
about that thing I wanted to ask you over the phone the other day,

214
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:56,980
I was thinking...

215
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,140
and...

216
00:14:58,140 --> 00:15:00,460
why do you think it is I got dumped?

217
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,080
Hi.

218
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:05,900
May I take your order?

219
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:06,900
Yes.

220
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:09,520
I'll have the fluffy souffle pancakes and an iced tea.

221
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:11,700
And she'll just have a glass of water.

222
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:12,780
Oh, so mean!

223
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:18,020
I'll have the same thing.

224
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:20,900
Two orders of pancakes and iced tea is coming right up.

225
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:23,980
Oh, Akane.

226
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,600
I have to say I'm disappointed in you.

227
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:26,960
What?

228
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:27,420
Why?

229
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,360
There's something I want to talk to you about.

230
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:29,800
Really?

231
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,200
Whoa, hold on.

232
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,200
Let's talk in person

233
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:34,320
so we can have a sit-down, meaningful chat.

234
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:37,060
While I waited a whole week for you

235
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:39,100
to make a full recovery from your cold,

236
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:41,180
I wasn't able to focus on anything else.

237
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:44,260
Going on three group dates was about all I could manage.

238
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:46,720
Yet now that I'm finally hearing from you,

239
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,620
you've decided to shatter my fantasies

240
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:50,800
by starting this off with the lamest opening ever.

241
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:51,860
It's disappointing.

242
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:53,440
Three group dates in a week

243
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,020
sounds like full throttle, doesn't it?

244
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:56,900
I've been patiently waiting

245
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,380
to hear some fun girl talk, sister!

246
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:59,640
Hey, come on.

247
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:00,720
Hear me out, will you?

248
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,160
Recently,

249
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:05,940
there's been something I can't get off my mind.

250
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:08,300
I want to figure it out.

251
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,480
You know, in a romantic sense.

252
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,900
In order for me to fully move on from this,

253
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:15,440
I need to know if I have any major flaws,

254
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:16,040
and if so,

255
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,840
I'd like to do what I can to fix them.

256
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:19,980
Like, maybe I have this obnoxious habit,

257
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:22,340
but I'm completely oblivious and don't realize it.

258
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,700
Where are these thoughts coming from?

259
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,120
It's like, no matter who I end up falling in love with,

260
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:27,380
it's something I got to fix.

261
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,540
And when I think that it might be a fatal flaw,

262
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:30,480
it terrifies me.

263
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:31,800
You don't have one.

264
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:34,060
If I knew I'd agonize about it,

265
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,280
then instead of avoiding it,

266
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:38,380
maybe I should have swallowed my pride that day

267
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:39,600
and asked Takuma why.

268
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,060
No, girl.

269
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,580
That's not the move.

270
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:43,920
Welcome.

271
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:47,080
Oh, hey!

272
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:48,920
Excuse me, sir.

273
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:50,500
I thought I saw a knockout in here,

274
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,720
and it turns out it's you, Momo.

275
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:54,200
Wow, what a coincidence.

276
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:56,120
Who are they?

277
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:58,200
They're from my group date two days ago.

278
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:00,720
They're super pesky and super touchy-feely,

279
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:03,040
so I dipped from there ASAP, but...

280
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:05,580
Why are you even going on group dates with guys like them?

281
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,820
Well, I met him through a friend of a friend, okay?

282
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:09,160
I'm a sit.

283
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,060
That's cool, yeah?

284
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:11,720
No, not cool at all!

285
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,640
Oh, you must be Momo's friend.

286
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:14,280
Hey there.

287
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:15,180
What trick you have.

288
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:16,380
I'm so sorry about this.

289
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,480
Momo will deal with them,

290
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,040
so you can just ignore them, Akane.

291
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,460
Don't you think you're being a little pushy?

292
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,340
Momo doesn't know what to do.

293
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:27,660
Yeah, I guess we're making a lot of trouble for you, aren't we?

294
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:29,020
You know, Momo,

295
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:31,480
you skipped out on paying for your drinks the other day.

296
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:33,880
Actually, I gave what I owe to the organizer,

297
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:34,880
thank you very much.

298
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:35,380
Really?

299
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:36,900
Well, that sure is news to me.

300
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:39,100
Did you even think to check with her yourself?

301
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,600
Oh, come on now.

302
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,020
Who cares about a few drinks?

303
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,140
Let's all just get along.

304
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:43,780
What do you say?

305
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:47,240
They're not going anywhere anytime soon, are they?

306
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,800
Whoa, Momo, your perfume smells awesome.

307
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:50,640
Nuh-uh, no way!

308
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:51,540
Personal space!

309
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:52,600
Hey, leave her alone!

310
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:53,420
Thank you for waiting.

311
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:54,380
Huh?

312
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:58,380
You ordered the fluffy souffle pancakes and iced tea, right?

313
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:00,820
Huh?

314
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:02,360
That's bizarre.

315
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:03,760
We have four guests now.

316
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:04,700
Who are they?

317
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:05,640
E-Eita!

318
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:06,600
Sasaki!

319
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:08,560
Actually, this table...

320
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:10,860
These guys came in and started bothering them.

321
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,300
Oh my goodness.

322
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:14,700
Yeah, these girls are friends of ours.

323
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,640
So don't give it another thought.

324
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:23,600
Excuse me, gentlemen.

325
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:27,300
I do apologize, but you appear to be inconveniencing these other customers.

326
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,360
So please, allow me to show you to a different table.

327
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:30,980
No thanks.

328
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,260
We're fine right here.

329
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:38,540
Apologies for the misunderstanding, sirs.

330
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:40,640
But you are inconveniencing these other customers.

331
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:43,100
So please relocate to another table.

332
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:45,320
Nah, man, I'm saying we're...

333
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:47,020
Your cooperation...

334
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:47,980
Is appreciated.

335
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:50,780
Uh...

336
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:55,100
Thank you so much, Eita.

337
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:56,540
Small world, huh?

338
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:57,780
Yeah, what a surprise.

339
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,320
I had no idea you worked here.

340
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:00,760
Well, I certainly noticed you.

341
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,580
Huh, you should have said something.

342
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,080
Well, keeping quiet was more...

343
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:05,020
They know each other?

344
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:06,480
Uh, excuse me.

345
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:09,680
I'm really sorry for having caused a commotion in your cafe.

346
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:10,880
Hmm?

347
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:12,940
No worries.

348
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:17,560
Man, what a shock.

349
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,700
Thank goodness Eita was here to make them go away.

350
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,140
That guy is incredibly good-looking, isn't he?

351
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:25,260
That's Eita.

352
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:26,780
He's another one of my guildmates.

353
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:27,100
Yup.

354
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:28,140
Huh?

355
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:28,940
Him too?

356
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:29,900
Uh-huh.

357
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:31,400
He's actually our master.

358
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:44,560
More and more, this game that you're playing seems to be dreamier than my group dates.

359
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:45,420
You know what?

360
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:47,140
I'm starting to feel hopeless.

361
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:47,560
Hmm.

362
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:59,600
So Momo, about what I was asking you earlier...

363
00:20:00,460 --> 00:20:00,820
Hmm?

364
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:06,540
Good work out there today.

365
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:08,560
Yeah, good work.

366
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,720
Hey, Sasaki, do you have a sec?

367
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:11,780
Uh, no.

368
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,820
I'm off the clock and unavailable for the rest of the day.

369
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,860
This isn't about work, silly.

370
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:21,260
Me and some of the daytime staff are going out to karaoke, so you should come along.

371
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:23,040
I want to thank you for helping earlier.

372
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:23,920
My treat.

373
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,960
My kid's sister's waiting for me to come home, so I can't.

374
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:29,140
Siscon.

375
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:29,880
How rude.

376
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:33,020
I merely love her a bit excessively, so, uh, yes.

377
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:33,580
Siscon.

378
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:35,220
You just admitted it.

379
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:36,680
Good work.

380
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:43,760
Hey, Eita.

381
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:44,820
Hmm?

382
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:46,020
Huh?

383
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,720
The two of you haven't left?

384
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:49,080
What's up?

385
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:50,940
Why are you hanging around this place?

386
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:52,740
We were waiting for you.

387
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:55,740
Oh my, kinda like groupies.

388
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:56,780
He's a strange one.

389
00:20:56,780 --> 00:21:08,100
There's something that I wanted to talk to you about.

390
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:09,000
Is that okay?

391
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:09,160
Hmm?

392
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Okay, are you two ready to get going? Is everyone's equipment in tip-top shape?

393
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Yes. Yes! I have to show her what I'm made of!

394
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Equipment...

395
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Actually, Tsubaki, is the gear you have on different from mine?

396
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Wow, so cool! Is this stuff, like, super rare?

397
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Uh, n-no.

398
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,000
Hey, where did you pick those up? Huh? Huh?

399
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:27,000
I didn't pick them up somewhere. It's the first quest.

400
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
Right, right. Go on.

401
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Actually, since you leveled up your initial gear to the max affinits, you're the one with the super rare stuff.

402
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Hmm...

